recomp.patch - what the Godot side needs changed in tools/recomp (rt, render, sound, app).
tools/godot/build.py applies it to its snapshot (`snapshot`), and writes it again from the snapshot (`patch`: the text
up to the first "diff -ru" line - these notes - is kept).  From the workspace root:
    patch -p1 -d tools/recomp --dry-run < tools/godot/recomp.patch

What is in it, and what the coordinator has to do with each:

1. sound/audio_out.cpp - the sound device is the host (RTA_AUDIO_HOST: tools/godot/lib/audio_host.inc).  Only the
   library is compiled with the macro; nothing changes for rta_app.  Since the first round.

2. sound/drivers.cpp - THE MUSIC'S OWN VOLUME: the HUD agent's hunk, taken as it is from tools/godot/hud-recomp.patch
   (rta_sound_set_music_gain; stream 2 of the stream driver is the music).  The library hands it out as
   rtag_set_option("music_volume", "0..1") when the core has it (build.py looks for the function's name).

3. THE GAME'S OWN HUD, SECOND GROUP (the boss meter and one-line message, the prompt box) - four files here and
   TWO LINES THAT ARE NOT IN THIS PATCH because they change the translation:
       tools/recomp/hle.txt, after "1dd270   # hud_spellSelect":
           1d93b0   # hud_drawBossMeter: the boss meter and the one-line message (a host with its own HUD can leave them out: Gs::hide_text)
           1d99f0   # hud_drawPromptBox: the interaction prompt's box (also the spell selector's)
   then the game has to be translated and compiled again (tools/recomp/app/build.py, and --original).
   In this patch: render/layout.h (a mark M_TEXT = 5, laid out as unmarked 2-D things are), render/gs.h and gs.cpp
   (Gs::hide_text: primitives under that mark, drawn into the 3-D buffer without a depth test, are left out),
   app/gfx_rt.cpp (the two wrappers, `Scope s(M_TEXT)`, as the five HUD draws are wrapped).
   ORDER MATTERS: gfx_rt.cpp's two wrappers define fn_001d93b0 / fn_001d99f0, which the translation itself defines
   until the two addresses are in hle.txt - applied without the hle.txt lines the link fails with duplicate symbols.
   A build whose translation lacks them defines RTA_NO_HUD_TEXT_HOOKS (tools/godot/build.py does so by itself: it
   looks for orig_001d93b0 in the translation's funcs.h).  The library's switch is rtag_set_option("game_hud_text",
   "off"), refused while the translation lacks the hooks.
   Ran here in a stand-in root (local/godot-spike/root: the shared tree with the two lines, translated again).

diff -ru recomp.orig/app/gfx_rt.cpp recomp/app/gfx_rt.cpp
--- recomp.orig/app/gfx_rt.cpp
+++ recomp/app/gfx_rt.cpp
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 const u32 G_CAMERA_MATRIX = 0x44F110;
 const u32 RAM_MASK = 0x01FFFFFF;                    // the display list is addressed through the 0x30000000 mirror of main memory
 
-enum Mode : u16 { M_NONE = 0, M_EDGE = 1, M_WORLD = 2, M_BILLBOARD = 3, M_MENU3D = 4 };
+enum Mode : u16 { M_NONE = 0, M_EDGE = 1, M_WORLD = 2, M_BILLBOARD = 3, M_MENU3D = 4, M_TEXT = 5 };
 
 std::atomic<bool> g_marks_always{false};    // set_hud_marks: the marks also at 4:3
 std::atomic<float> g_wanted{1.0f};      // k = (4/3) / aspect the application asks for
@@ -295,6 +295,14 @@
 void fn_001df720(Ctx* c) { Scope s(M_EDGE); orig_001df720(c); }
 void fn_001e42e0(Ctx* c) { Scope s(M_EDGE); orig_001e42e0(c); }
 void fn_001dd270(Ctx* c) { Scope s(M_EDGE); orig_001dd270(c); }
+#ifndef RTA_NO_HUD_TEXT_HOOKS
+// hud_drawBossMeter (the boss meter and the one-line message) and hud_drawPromptBox (the interaction prompt, also
+// the spell selector's): marked so that a host that draws its own can leave them out (Gs::hide_text).  Their layout
+// is the unmarked one.  Needs 1d93b0 and 1d99f0 in hle.txt; a build whose translation lacks them defines
+// RTA_NO_HUD_TEXT_HOOKS (tools/godot/build.py does, by itself).
+void fn_001d93b0(Ctx* c) { Scope s(M_TEXT); orig_001d93b0(c); }
+void fn_001d99f0(Ctx* c) { Scope s(M_TEXT); orig_001d99f0(c); }
+#endif
 void fn_001907d0(Ctx* c) { Scope s(M_BILLBOARD); orig_001907d0(c); }
 void fn_0018fe18(Ctx* c) { Scope s(M_BILLBOARD); orig_0018fe18(c); }
 void fn_001c1108(Ctx* c) { Scope s(M_MENU3D); g_menu_view++; orig_001c1108(c); g_menu_view--; }
